// Zero-padding an Int. The rows pin, in order: a single digit padded; zero
// padded; a negative value where the sign counts toward the width; a value
// already wider than the width, returned unpadded rather than truncated; and
// a negative width, which the early return clamps.
fn main() {
    println((7).pad(2))
    println((0).pad(2))
    println((-5).pad(3))
    println((123).pad(2))
    println((7).pad(-1))
}
